Equity risk is the risk of loss because of a drop in the market price of shares. *(volatility)* 

Equity risk arises from *fluctuations in the share price* and the risk of the *issuer defaulting*. It is considered as a #voir("market-risk").

Equity risk often refers to *equity investment risk*, which is the risk associated with the investment in shares/stocks of a company due to *company-specific factors* (e.g., rising cost of inputs, strategic weaknesses, etc.). In this case the equity risk is a #voir("specific-risk").

Market risk cannot be diversified away, while specific risk can be mitigated by holding assets with less than perfect correlations.